            <div class="prose max-w-none" x-show="lang === 'en'" x-cloak>
                <p>Budget allocation is the make-or-break decision for any new e-commerce store going global. Here's a practical checklist to guide you from cold start through to stable growth.</p>
<h2>Phase 1: Cold Start (Weeks 1-4) — Test First, Scale Later</h2>
<p>Your goal is validating which channels work, not chasing revenue.</p>
<h3>Budget Allocation</h3>
<ul>
<li><strong>Meta Ads: 40-50%</strong><br />
  Test 3-5 ad sets with different interest audiences and lookalikes using varied creative directions</li>
<li><strong>Google Performance Max: 30-40%</strong><br />
  Feed sufficient conversion events so the algorithm can learn effectively</li>
<li><strong>TikTok Video Ads: 10-20%</strong><br />
  Focus on creative testing, not ROI — prioritize watch completion and click-through rates</li>
<li><strong>Reserve for Testing: 5-10%</strong><br />
  Allocate for experimenting with new formats or platforms</li>
</ul>
<h3>Weekly Checklist</h3>
<ul>
<li>[ ] Verify Pixel/SDK installation and confirm conversion events are firing correctly</li>
<li>[ ] Set minimum daily budget of $20 per ad set (gives algorithm room to learn)</li>
<li>[ ] Keep concurrent ad sets under 10 to avoid budget dilution</li>
<li>[ ] Log data for first 3 days of each ad set to spot anomalies</li>
<li>[ ] Review account daily for any unusual spend</li>
</ul>
<h3>Target Metrics</h3>
<table>
<thead>
<tr>
<th>Metric</th>
<th>Benchmark</th>
</tr>
</thead>
<tbody>
<tr>
<td>Cost Per Click (CPC)</td>
<td>Under 1.5x category average</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>Add-to-Cart Rate</td>
<td>&gt;5%</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>Checkout Initiation</td>
<td>&gt;3%</td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table>
<hr />
<h2>Phase 2: Growth (Weeks 5-12) — Double Down on What Works</h2>
<p>Found profitable ads? Now concentrate budget on high performers while continuously testing new creatives.</p>
<h3>Budget Allocation</h3>
<ul>
<li><strong>Top Performing Campaigns: 60-70%</strong><br />
  Shift 80% of budget to your top 2 campaigns by ROAS</li>
<li><strong>New Campaign Testing: 20-30%</strong><br />
  Keep exploring new audiences, creatives, and landing pages</li>
<li><strong>Retargeting: 10-15%</strong><br />
  Dedicated budget for cart abandoners and website visitors</li>
</ul>
<h3>Weekly Checklist</h3>
<ul>
<li>[ ] Every Monday, rank channels by ROAS and pause any underperforming at 50% of target</li>
<li>[ ] Launch at least 2 new creative sets weekly</li>
<li>[ ] Maintain minimum $50 daily budget per ad set for stable delivery</li>
<li>[ ] Use budget rules to automatically shift spend to top performers</li>
<li>[ ] Audit lookalike seed quality — exclude low-value customers</li>
</ul>
<h3>Common Mistake: Scaling Too Fast</h3>
<p>A home goods store hit 4.0 ROAS in week 6 and immediately increased daily budget from $100 to $500. CPC doubled and ROAS crashed to 1.8.</p>
<p><strong>Right approach</strong>: Never increase budget by more than 30% per day. Allow 2-3 days for the algorithm to relearn between scaling steps.</p>
<hr />
<h2>Phase 3: Stable (Week 13+) — Reduce Acquisition Dependency</h2>
<p>Relying solely on paid traffic is risky. Shift focus to customer retention and organic growth.</p>
<h3>Budget Allocation</h3>
<ul>
<li><strong>Performance Ads: 50-60% of budget</strong><br />
  Shift from growth mode to profitability protection</li>
<li><strong>Retargeting: 15-20%</strong><br />
  Prioritize reactivating existing customers over new acquisition</li>
<li><strong>Brand Search: 10-15%</strong><br />
  Defend branded search from competitors</li>
<li><strong>Content/SEO: 10-15%</strong><br />
  Build long-tail content to establish organic traffic</li>
</ul>
<h3>Monthly Checklist</h3>
<ul>
<li>[ ] Calculate LTV/CAC ratio monthly — target LTV/CAC &gt; 3</li>
<li>[ ] Email list should reach 20% of total ad reach</li>
<li>[ ] Repeat purchase rate exceeds 30%</li>
<li>[ ] Monitor month-over-month branded search volume trends</li>
<li>[ ] Track organic traffic growth as percentage of total</li>
</ul>
<hr />
<h2>Universal Rules for All Phases</h2>
<ol>
<li><strong>Always reserve 10-15% for testing</strong> — the market evolves constantly</li>
<li><strong>Never operate a single ad account</strong> — one account failure means cash flow crisis</li>
<li><strong>Limit daily budget swings to 30%</strong> — volatility disrupts algorithm learning</li>
<li><strong>Reconcile weekly</strong> — verify spend matches plan and catch anomalies early</li>
</ol>
<hr />
<p><strong>Bottom line</strong>: There's no universal budget formula, but there is a universal rhythm: test channels during cold start, concentrate火力 during growth, and reduce acquisition dependency in the stable phase. Follow this checklist and you'll avoid 80% of common budget allocation mistakes.</p>
